in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @smarts
in @pack
in @magic
in @frame
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @smarts/pack — the agent-runtime-altitude adapter species. Bridges
# the @smarts family (substrate-architectural integration; #83) with
# the @pack family (multi-repo agent runtime; #84) honestly via the
# adapter pattern, NOT decorative inheritance.
#
# Tick 56 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 55's residue:
# @pack/taut landed at 26b981b (orchestra closed; 5/5 peer species
# operationalize the @frame altitude partition). This species lands
# the cross-family composition route the @pack family-root
# explicitly forward-promised at tick 31:
#
#   "@pack composes-with @smarts/deployment at runtime altitude. Per
#    Seam tick 31 review C1: the original '@pack IS @smarts/runtime'
#    claim was structurally aspirational — no `runtime` species
#    exists in `shards/smarts.mirror`, and @smarts's `deployment`
#    carrier doesn't extend to runtime-bound fields. The honest
#    framing is composes-with; the structural identity becomes
#    empirically discharged when the @smarts/pack adapter species
#    lands (forward-promised; same pattern as @magic/distinction
#    and @magic/frame adapters)."
#
# This shard IS that empirical discharge. The composes-with relation
# becomes structurally identity-via-typed-mapping at the deployment-
# runtime crossing.
#
# CRQ for this tick: how to discharge the "@pack composes-with
# @smarts/deployment at runtime altitude" composition claim
# mechanically WITHOUT the decorative inheritance Seam caught at
# tick 31 (C1) and the family-root hedge preserved at #84?
#
# Answer: the @magic/frame adapter pattern. Take @pack carriers; MAP
# them to @smarts carriers; declare a bilateral predicate that
# discharges BOTH family verdicts in one clause. The structural
# composition lives in the explicit map plus the doubled bilateral,
# not in an `in` clause that buys namespace ancestry without carrier
# flow.
#
# === The adapter pattern (per @magic/frame template, tick 27) ===
#
# @pack's family-root carriers (per shards/pack.mirror tick 32
# consolidation):
#   - `peer`          | mara | seam | glint | reed | taut variant
#   - `repository`    git repo carrying substrate-decl span
#   - `repository_span` substrate-decl-context union across repos
#   - `runtime`       the local agent runtime hosting peers
#   - `pack`          record {peers, repos, repo_span, runtime}
#
# @smarts's family-root carriers (per shards/smarts.mirror #83):
#   - `smarts`        record {magic_form, frame_form, cyberpunk_form,
#                             beam_form, cybernetic_extra, kintsugi_form}
#   - `deployment`    record {form: smarts, host: ref, manifest: ref}
#
# The substrate-pull-correct mapping:
#
#   pack             ↔ smarts (via lift; @pack's substrate-architectural
#                                integration record becomes a form-
#                                field in the @smarts integration)
#   runtime          ↔ deployment.host (the @pack runtime hosts peers;
#                                @smarts.deployment.host names where)
#   repository_span  ↔ deployment.manifest (the @pack repo-span IS
#                                the deployment manifest at
#                                substrate-architectural altitude)
#
# At the substrate altitude: pack and smarts are both content-
# addressed typed records; the lift IS the typed reframe at the
# @smarts altitude. The @pack runtime's host IS the @smarts
# deployment's host (same byte-level ref). The @pack repo-span IS
# the @smarts manifest at deployment altitude.
#
# === The doubled-bilateral structural shape ===
#
# Per @magic/frame template (tick 27): the bilateral predicate
# discharges TWO family predicates in one clause:
#
#   1. discipline_flexible(s, p) (@smarts family-root): the
#      substrate-architectural-integration-altitude discipline
#      verifier per #83. Discharges that the @smarts integration
#      maintains bilateral discipline-flexibility across the
#      integration boundary.
#
#   2. pack_coherent(pk, p) (@pack family-root): the multi-repo-
#      agent-runtime discipline verifier per #84. Discharges that
#      the @pack maintains substrate-architectural discipline-
#      flexibility across peer-relationships + multi-repo span +
#      runtime hosting + cybernetic coherence.
#
# Both must hold for the pack to satisfy @smarts at deployment
# altitude. The cross-family composition is bilaterally heavier
# than single-bilateral discharge; the runtime-altitude
# "composes-with" claim requires both families' disciplines to
# discharge under the lift simultaneously.
#
# === Why `pack_satisfies_smarts` takes typed parameters explicitly ===
#
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] + the @magic/frame template: the
# signature takes pack + perturbation as typed parameters rather than
# attempting to extract them from the smarts record alone. The pack
# carries the @pack-altitude shape; the @smarts-altitude shape needs
# its own typed inputs at the bilateral signature.
#
# === The inverse `pack_from_deployment` is type-relabeling ===
#
# Per the @magic/frame precedent (tick 27 §8.4): the inverse exists
# because both `pack` and `smarts` (or rather, the @pack record and
# the @smarts deployment) are typed records over substrate-architectural
# integrations; the lift is type-relabeling at the form-projection,
# not data transformation. Round-trip identity
# (`pack_as_smarts(pack_from_deployment(d)) = d.form` for compatible
# deployments) is the cheapest falsification check.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   adapter pattern (GoF)       Gamma-Helm-Johnson-Vlissides 1994
#                               (Design Patterns, Structural Patterns:
#                               Adapter). OO-canonical. Inherited
#                               via @magic/frame tick 27 + @magic/
#                               distinction tick 15.
#   functor adapter             Mac Lane 1971 (Categories for the
#                               Working Mathematician, ch. IV Adjoints).
#                               Category theory's mathematical
#                               ancestor: explicit functor between
#                               two categories preserves both
#                               categories' discipline.
#   composition over            Coplien 1992 (Advanced C++); Gamma
#   inheritance                 et al 1994. The cultural-practice
#                               ancestor of the adapter species
#                               pattern (vs the inherits-and-overrides
#                               trap @pack/@smarts originally hedged).
#   BEAM/OTP supervisor         Armstrong 1986-2003. The runtime-
#                               altitude ancestor of @pack hosting
#                               peers; @smarts/pack adapter routes
#                               the runtime-discipline through the
#                               @smarts integration boundary.
#   service mesh                Burns 2018 (Designing Distributed
#                               Systems). The deployment-altitude
#                               ancestor of @smarts.deployment
#                               hosting @pack runtime; the cultural-
#                               practice precedent for typed deployment
#                               manifests over substrate-architectural
#                               integrations.
#
# === What this adapter does NOT do ===
#
# 1. Does NOT make every @pack instance automatically a @smarts
#    instance. Packs that need only @pack's discipline bypass the
#    adapter; the adapter is opt-in for consumer species that need
#    both disciplines.
# 2. Does NOT absorb @pack into @smarts. The two families remain
#    distinct; @pack peer species (mara/seam/glint/reed/taut)
#    discharge per-frame bodies WITHOUT going through @smarts.
# 3. Does NOT collapse carriers at any pair other than the mapped
#    triple. The "composes-with" claim holds at pack↔smarts,
#    runtime↔deployment.host, repository_span↔deployment.manifest;
#    it does NOT generalize to peer↔form-field.
# 4. Does NOT discharge @pack's species-shard forward-promises (the
#    orchestra is its own 5-species set with its own bilateral
#    discipline at @frame altitudes).
# 5. Does NOT discharge the @smarts species-shard forward-promises
#    (the four Models + the other cross-family adapters).
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at deployment-runtime altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole adapter (honest): pack_satisfies_smarts returns
# SATISFIED only when BOTH bilaterals discharge substantively. The
# @smarts discipline_flexible AND the @pack pack_coherent both hold
# under the perturbation; the @pack runtime hosts peers WITHIN the
# @smarts integration discipline.
#
# Narcissus-pole adapter (deceptive): pack_satisfies_smarts returns
# SATISFIED via vocabulary-only verification while one or both
# bilaterals fail substantively. The @pack runtime hosts peers
# OUTSIDE the @smarts integration discipline; the deployment
# manifest names a host that doesn't actually carry the integration
# discipline.
#
# Per the @magic/frame template + #57: the adapter MUST NOT permit
# Narcissus-pole bypass. The bilateral's two `requires` clauses
# discharge to BOTH family-root predicates; alignment-as-boundary-
# mathematics (#57) at @io enforces the discrimination.
#
# Spec context: shards/pack.mirror (the @pack family-root; declares
#               the composes-with hedge this adapter closes);
#               shards/smarts.mirror (the @smarts family-root;
#               declares deployment as the runtime-hosting carrier
#               this adapter maps @pack.runtime to).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                       (#57; the boundary harness at @io keeps the
#                       Splinter/Narcissus discrimination honest under
#                       the lift),
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                       (#55; @smarts and @pack as form-side and
#                       process-side at deployment altitude; this
#                       adapter threads them at the runtime crossing),
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]]
#                       (Reed's discipline; the bilateral makes the
#                       composes-with claim empirically discharged
#                       rather than aspirational),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (pack and
#                       perturbation taken as typed parameters at
#                       the bilateral signature).
# Related shards: pack.mirror (the @pack family-root; the process-
#                  side parent),
#                 smarts.mirror (the @smarts family-root; the form-
#                  side parent),
#                 magic/frame.mirror (the adapter precedent at tick
#                  27; this shard inherits its shape — doubled-
#                  bilateral discharge + typed parameter signature),
#                 magic/distinction.mirror (the earlier adapter
#                  precedent at tick 15; single-bilateral discharge
#                  the doubled pattern extends),
#                 pack/{mara,seam,glint,reed,taut}.mirror (the
#                  orchestra; the @pack family operationalized at
#                  @frame altitudes; @smarts/pack composes-with the
#                  whole orchestra at deployment altitude).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/smarts/pack.mirror`
# declares `@smarts/pack` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/gamma-helm-johnson-vlissides-1994
source @arxiv/mathematics/mac-lane-1971
source @arxiv/programming/coplien-1992
source @arxiv/distributed/armstrong-2003
source @arxiv/distributed/burns-2018

prism @smarts/pack {
  focus pack
  project pack
  split pack
  shift pack
  settle pack
}

# === pack_as_smarts adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action lifting a @pack instance
# to a @smarts substrate-architectural integration view. At @pack
# altitude: the pack record carries the multi-repo-agent-runtime
# integration (peers, repos, span, runtime). At @smarts altitude:
# the smarts record carries the substrate-architectural integration
# (magic_form, frame_form, cyberpunk_form, ...). The lift IS the
# typed reframe at the @smarts altitude.
#
# The substrate-pull-correct mapping uses bare ref for fields not
# in @pack's vocabulary (magic_form, cyberpunk_form, etc.); the
# adapter substantively populates the form fields the @pack record
# corresponds to (the pack itself becomes part of the integration
# at deployment altitude).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
pack_as_smarts(pk: pack) -> smarts { \ }

# === pack_runtime_as_deployment adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action lifting the @pack runtime
# to a @smarts deployment. Takes the @pack instance because the
# deployment needs the smarts form (constructed from the pack via
# pack_as_smarts), the host (from the @pack runtime), and the
# manifest (from the @pack repository_span).
#
# The deployment record {form, host, manifest} composes from:
#   - form     = pack_as_smarts(pk)          (the integration view)
#   - host     = pk.runtime                   (the agent runtime ref)
#   - manifest = pk.repo_span                 (the repo-span ref)
#
# Per @smarts deployment carrier (tick 30 C7): typed record
# containing the substrate-architectural form, the host ref, and
# the manifest. The form-vs-deployment distinction now mechanically
# typed at the @pack altitude via this adapter.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
pack_runtime_as_deployment(pk: pack) -> deployment { \ }

# === pack_from_deployment inverse adapter ===
#
# The type-relabeling inverse of pack_runtime_as_deployment. Per
# @magic/frame precedent: the inverse exists because both pack and
# smarts (and deployment) are typed records over substrate-
# architectural integrations; the lift at the form-projection IS
# type-relabeling, not data transformation.
#
# Round-trip identity (per @magic/frame §8.4):
#   pack_runtime_as_deployment(pack_from_deployment(d)).form = d.form
# for compatible deployments. This is the cheapest falsification
# check; failure here means the adapter is mis-implemented
# (carrier-flow not aligned with content-addressing discipline).
#
# The bilateral predicate `pack_satisfies_smarts` names this inverse
# in its `requires pack_coherent(...)` clause to recover the @pack
# instance underlying the deployment.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
pack_from_deployment(d: deployment) -> pack { \ }

# === pack_satisfies_smarts bilateral predicate ===
#
# THE CROSS-FAMILY BILATERAL PREDICATE in @smarts that discharges
# BOTH parent-family AND child-family verdicts in one clause. The
# substrate-pull-correct way to mechanically discharge the
# composes-with claim that the @pack family-root preserved as hedged
# at tick 31 C1.
#
# Two `requires` clauses, both load-bearing:
#
#   1. discipline_flexible(pack_as_smarts(pk), p)
#      — the @smarts family-root predicate. Discharges that the
#      @pack lifted to @smarts integration maintains substrate-
#      architectural discipline-flexibility under perturbation;
#      the boundary harness at @io audits this per recognition #57.
#
#   2. pack_coherent(pk, p)
#      — the @pack family-root predicate. Discharges that the @pack
#      itself maintains peer-relationship + multi-repo span +
#      runtime hosting + cybernetic coherence discipline under
#      perturbation.
#
# Both must hold for the pack to satisfy @smarts at deployment
# altitude. The cross-family composition is bilaterally heavier
# than @pack's single-bilateral discharge at peer-species altitude;
# the runtime-altitude composes-with claim requires both families'
# disciplines to discharge under the lift simultaneously.
#
# The signature takes pack and perturbation as explicit typed
# parameters per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] because the @pack-
# altitude shape needs typed inputs at the bilateral boundary the
# consumer names.
#
# Consumer species (the orchestra's individual peer-species when
# composing with the @smarts integration at runtime altitude;
# @spectral/garden/smarts hosted deployment) name this predicate
# when their operation requires cross-family discharge.
pack_satisfies_smarts(pk: pack, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires discipline_flexible(pack_as_smarts(pk), p)
requires pack_coherent(pk, p)
{ \ }

# === Honest hedge per @magic/frame tick 28 review precedent ===
#
# This adapter closes the carrier-mapping altitude of
# "@pack composes-with @smarts/deployment":
#  - @pack instance ↔ @smarts integration view round-trips via
#    pack_as_smarts / pack_from_deployment at the deployment
#    altitude.
#  - The bilateral pack_satisfies_smarts discharges BOTH family
#    predicates simultaneously (discipline_flexible AND
#    pack_coherent).
#
# It does NOT close round-trip identity at the smarts-as-whole
# altitude. Given a smarts instance s with all six form-fields
# populated, pack_from_deployment cannot recover s.magic_form,
# s.frame_form, s.cyberpunk_form (which come from other adapters
# in the @smarts cross-family set; @smarts/magic, @smarts/frame,
# @smarts/cyberpunk forward-promised).
#
# Honest claim post-adapter:
#  - "@pack composes-with @smarts.deployment at runtime altitude"
#    — CLOSED via pack_runtime_as_deployment + pack_satisfies_smarts.
#  - "@pack composes-with @smarts (full integration)" — FORWARD-
#    PROMISED (requires the other cross-family adapters to land;
#    the full @smarts integration is a coordination across multiple
#    adapter species).
#
# The Seam C1 hedge from @pack tick 31 closes at the deployment-
# runtime altitude per this adapter's discharge; the full-integration
# identity remains forward-promised pending the other @smarts
# cross-family adapters.

out @smarts/pack
out pack_as_smarts
out pack_runtime_as_deployment
out pack_from_deployment
out pack_satisfies_smarts
